"Let the two consecutive perfect squares be \\( n^2 \\) and \\( (n+1)^2 \\). The positive difference between these two squares is given by:\n\n\\[\n(n+1)^2 - n^2 = 35\n\\]\n\nExpanding the left-hand side, we get:\n\n\\[\nn^2 + 2n + 1 - n^2 = 35\n\\]\n\nSimplifying, we have:\n\n\\[\n2n + 1 = 35\n\\]\n\nSubtracting 1 from both sides, we get:\n\n\\[\n2n = 34\n\\]\n\nDividing both sides by  we, we find:\n\n\\[\nn = 17\n\\]\n\nThus, the two consecutive perfect squares are \\( 17^2 \\) and \\( 18^2 \\). Calculating these, we get:\n\n\\[\n17^2 = 289 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 18^2 = 324\n\\]\n\nThe greater of the two squares is 324. Therefore, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{324}\\)."
"To solve the problem, we need to find the value of \\( A \\) such that \\( A \\ \\spadesuit \\ 2 = 19 \\). Given the operation \\( A \\ \\spadesuit \\ B = A + B + 4 \\), we can substitute \\( B = 2 \\) into the equation:\n\n\\[ A \\ \\spadesuit \\ 2 = A + 2 + 4 \\]\n\nSimplifying this, we get:\n\n\\[ A \\ \\spadesuit \\ 2 = A + 6 \\]\n\nWe are given that \\( A \\ \\spadesuit \\ 2 = 19 \\), so we can set up the equation:\n\n\\[ A + 6 = 19 \\]\n\nTo find \\( A \\), we need to isolate \\( on one side of the equation. We do this by subtracting 6 from both sides:\n\n\\[ A + 6 - 6 = 19 - 6 \\]\n\nSimplifying both sides, we get:\n\n\\[ A = 13 \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( A \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{13}\n\\]"
"To determine the cost to carpet a floor that is \\(16 \\times 13\\) square feet, we first need to find the constant of proportionality. We know that the cost is directly proportional to the area, so we can use the given information to find the constant.\n\nThe area of the first floor is \\(14 \\times 5 = 70\\) square feet, and the cost to carpet it is $105. Therefore, the constant of proportionality \\(k\\) is:\n\\[ k = \\frac{105}{70} = 1.5 \\]\n\nNow, we use this constant to find the cost to carpet the floor that is \\(16 \\times 13\\) square feet. The area of this floor is \\(16 \\times 13 = 20.8\\) square feet. The cost to carpet this floor is:\n\\[ \\text{Cost} = 1.5 \\times 20.8 = 31.2 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nTherefore, the cost to carpet the floor that is \\(16 \\times 13\\) square feet is \\(\\boxed{312}\\) dollars."
