"The binomial coefficient $\\dbinom{1001}{2}$ is calculated as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\dbinom{1001}{2} = \\frac{1001!}{2!(1001-2)!} = \\frac{1001!}{2! \\cdot 999!}\n\\]\n\nWe can simplify this by canceling out the common terms in the numerator and the denominator:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1001!}{2! \\cdot 999!} = \\frac{1001 \\times 1000 \\times 999!}{2! \\times 999!} = \\frac{1001 \\times 1000}{2}\n\\]\n\nNow, we perform the division:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1001 \\times 1000}{2} = 1001 \\times 500 = 500500\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of $\\dbinom{1001}{2}$ is \\( \\boxed{500,500}\\)."
