"To find the probability that the top two cards are both Aces, we need to consider the total number of ways to choose 2 cards from the deck and the number of ways to choose 2 Aces.\n\nFirst, we calculate the total number of ways to choose 2 cards from 52:\n\\[\n\\binom{52}{2} = \\frac{52 \\times 51}{2 \\times 1} = 1326\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the number of ways to choose 2 Aces from the 4 Aces in the deck:\n\\[\n\\binom{4}{2} = \\frac{4 \\times 3}{2 \\times 1} = 6\n\\]\n\nThe probability that the top two cards are both Aces is the ratio of the number of ways to choose 2 Aces to the total number of ways to choose 2 cards:\n\\[\n\\frac{6}{1326} = \\frac{1}{221}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the probability that the top two cards are both Aces is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{1}{221}}\n\\]"
