"We start by rewriting the given equation:\n\\[4x^3 - 41x^2 + 10x = 1989.\\]\n\nFirst, we try to factor the left-hand side. Notice that the coefficients of the polynomial are symmetric and can be factored in a specific form. We can use the fact that the polynomial can be factored as:\n\\[4x^3 - 41x^2 + 10x = (2x - 1)(2x^2 - 40x + 10).\\]\n\nNext, we factor the quadratic term:\n\\[2x^2 - 40x + 10 = (2x - 1)(2x - 10).\\]\n\nThus, the equation becomes:\n\\[(2x - 1)(2x - 10) = 1989.\\]\n\nWe observe that:\n\\[2x - 1 = 19.\\]\nSolving for \\(x\\), we get:\n\\[x = 10.\\]\n\nTherefore, the positive integer \\(x\\) that satisfies the equation is:\n\\[\\boxed{10}.\\]"
