"To determine whether \\( f(x) g(x) \\) is even, odd, or neither, we need to analyze the properties of \\( f(x) \\) and \\( g(x) \\).\n\nGiven:\n- \\( f(x) \\) is an even function, meaning \\( f(-x) = f(x) \\).\n- \\( g(x) \\) is an odd function, meaning \\( g(-x) = -g(x) \\).\n\nNow, consider the product \\( f(x) g(x) \\):\n\\[ f(-x) g(-x) = f(-x) (-g(-x)) \\]\n\nUsing the properties of \\( f(x) \\) and \\( g(x) \\):\n\\[ f(-x) g(-x) = f(x) (-g(x)) \\]\n\\[ f(-x) g(-x) = -f(x) g(x) \\]\n\nThis shows that \\( f(-x) g(-x) = -f(x) g(x) \\), which is the definition of an odd function.\n\nTherefore, \\( f(x) g(x) \\) is an odd function.\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{odd}}\\)."
