"First, we need to find the area of one of the smaller circles. The formula for the area of a circle is \\( A = \\pi r^2 \\), where \\( r \\) is the radius.\n\nFor a smaller circle with radius 4 inches:\n\\[ A = \\pi (4)^2 = 16\\pi \\text{ square inches} \\]\n\nSince there are four smaller circles, the total area of the four smaller circles is:\n\\[ 4 \\times 16\\pi = 64\\pi \\text{ square inches} \\]\n\nThe area of the larger circle is equal to the total area of the four smaller circles, which is \\( 64\\pi \\) square inches. Let \\( R \\) be the radius of the larger circle. The area of the larger circle is given by:\n\\[ \\pi R^2 = 64\\pi \\]\n\nDividing both sides by \\( \\pi \\):\n\\[ R^2 = 64 \\]\n\nTaking the square root of both sides:\n\\[ R = \\sqrt{64} = 8 \\]\n\nTherefore, the radius of the larger circle is \\( \\boxed{8} \\) inches."
