"First, we need to find the measure of an interior angle of a regular decagon. The sum of the interior angles of a polygon with \\( n \\) sides is given by:\n\n\\[\n(n-2) \\times 180^\\circ\n\\]\n\nFor a decagon (\\( n = 10 \\)):\n\n\\[\n(10-2) \\times 180^\\circ = 8 \\times 180^\\circ = 1440^\\circ\n\\]\n\nNext, we will find the measure of an interior angle of a regular pentagon. For a pentagon (\\( n = 5 \\)):\n\n\\[\n(5-2) \\times 180^\\circ = 3 \\times 180^\\circ = 540^\\circ\n\\]\n\nNow, we find the difference between the measure of an interior angle of a decagon and an interior angle of a pentagon:\n\n\\[\n1440^\\circ - 540^\\circ = 900^\\circ\n\\]\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is $\\boxed{900^\\circ}$. I hope it is correct."
