"We can express the line in parametric form as:\n\\[x = 2 + 3t, \\quad y = -1 + 4t, \\quad z = 2 + 12t.\\]\n\nSubstituting these into the plane equation $x - y + z = 5$, we get:\n\\[(2 + 3t) - (-1 + 4t) + (2 + 12t) = 5.\\]\n\nSimplifying, we have:\n\\[3 + 11t = 5.\\]\n\nSolving for $t$, we get:\n\\[11t = 2 \\Rightarrow t = \\frac{2}{11}.\\]\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection is:\n\\[(2 + 3 \\cdot \\frac{2}{11}, -1 + 4 \\cdot \\frac{2}{11}, 2 + 12 \\cdot \\frac{2}{11}) = \\boxed{(2.6, -0.2, 4)}.\\]\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is $(2.6, -0.2, 4)$. I hope it is correct."
