"We start by analyzing the given recurrence relation:\n\\[ a_{n+1} = a_n^3 - 3a_n^2 + 3. \\]\n\nWe need to find the values of \\( a_0 \\) such that \\( a_{2007} = a_0 \\). This implies that the sequence is periodic with period 2007.\n\nTo solve this, we need to find the fixed points of the sequence. A fixed point \\( a \\) satisfies:\n\\[ a = a^3 - 3a^2 + 3. \\]\n\nRearranging the equation, we get:\n\\[ a^3 - 3a^2 + 3a - 3 = 0. \\]\n\nThis can be factored as:\n\\[ (a - 1)^3 = 0. \\]\n\nThus, the only solution is:\n\\[ a = 1. \\]\n\nTherefore, the only value of \\( a_0 \\) where \\( a_{2007} = a_0 \\) is \\( a_0 = 1 \\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1}\n\\]"
"The volume of the parallelepiped generated by vectors \\(\\mathbf{a}\\), \\(\\mathbf{b}\\), and \\(\\mathbf{c}\\) is given by the scalar triple product \\(\\|\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c})\\|\\).\n\nWe know that:\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c})\\| = \\|\\mathbf{a}\\| \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| \\|\\mathbf{c}\\| \\cos \\theta\n\\]\nwhere \\(\\theta\\) is the angle between the vectors \\(\\mathbf{a}\\), \\(\\mathbf{b}\\), and \\(\\mathbf{c}\\).\n\nGiven:\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{a}\\| = \\|\\mathbf{b}\\| = \\|\\mathbf{c}\\| = 2\n\\]\n\\[\n\\cos \\theta = \\frac{5}{8}\n\\]\n\nSubstitute these values into the formula:\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{a} \\cdot (\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c})\\| = 2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 2 \\cdot \\frac{5}{8} = 8 \\cdot \\frac{5}{8} = 5\n\\]\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{5}\n\\]"
"The set \\( S \\) consists of all points \\((x, y, z)\\) such that \\( x^2 + y^2 + z^2 \\le 25 \\) and \\( z \\ge 0 \\). This describes a hemisphere of radius 5 centered at the origin, lying above the \\( xy \\)-plane.\n\nTo find the side length of the largest cube contained in \\( S \\), we need to consider the geometry of the hemisphere. The largest cube that can fit within this hemisphere will have its diagonal equal to the diameter of the hemisphere.\n\nThe diameter of the hemisphere is twice the radius, which is \\( 2 \\times 5 = 10 \\).\n\nThe diagonal of a cube with side length \\( s \\) is given by \\( s\\sqrt{3} \\). Setting this equal to the diameter of the hemisphere, we have:\n\n\\[ s\\sqrt{3} = 10 \\]\n\nSolving for \\( s \\):\n\n\\[ s = \\frac{10}{\\sqrt{3}} = 5\\sqrt{3} \\]\n\nTherefore, the side length of the largest cube contained in \\( S \\) is \\(\\boxed{\\{5\\sqrt{3}}\\)."
